docs/_intermediate.html
docs/_tw-output.css

# Second-layer backstop - ~/.config/bws/access-token (the bws/Secrets
# Manager machine-account token) is deliberately never chezmoi-managed and
# already blocked from `chezmoi add` by home/.chezmoiignore (verified: a
# real `chezmoi add`, even with `-r`/`--force`, skips it entirely). This
# just covers a copy landing in the tree some other way (e.g. hand-copied
# in) - matches on basename only, so it also catches chezmoi's
# private_/encrypted_-prefixed source names.
*access-token*

# Same idea for ~/.claude/.credentials.json (Claude Code's own OAuth
# token) - already blocked from `chezmoi add` by home/.chezmoiignore's
# default-deny .claude/** allowlist (verified with the real binary,
# including -r/--force), this is just the same basename-match backstop
# in case a copy ever lands in the tree some other way.
.credentials.json
